5. Sample Data
The seed script loads 70 student records. It also creates four lecturers, twelve teaching assistants, six courses, lecturer and TA assignments, course enrolments, fee invoices, and fee payments. The student records use the supplied student IDs and names. Because the supplied student data does not provide email addresses, the project generates student email addresses from student IDs as a project assumption.

6. Outstanding Fees Function
The database defines get_outstanding_fees(), a PL/pgSQL function that calculates the total amount due, total amount paid, and outstanding balance for every student. The function uses aggregated invoice and payment data and prevents a negative outstanding balance by applying a minimum value of zero. It returns the result as JSONB, which allows the web service to send the data directly to the application.

7. Supporting Database Features
• The student_fee_summary view provides a summarized fee position for each student.
• Indexes support common searches on student IDs in enrolments, payments, and invoices.
• Foreign keys maintain relationships between students, courses, staff, enrolments, invoices, and payments.
• Unique constraints prevent duplicate student-course, lecturer-course, and TA-course assignments.
• The cpen208_backup.sql file provides a database backup for restoration and submission.
